    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0358" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/637: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Mexico (Clark)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-08T18:00:00-05:00">February 8, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Your 35, February 6, 3 p.m.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d278-f1"/> When a suitable
                    opportunity offers you may express informally to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs the appreciation of the President and myself for the assurance on the
                    part of the Mexican Government that in case of difficulties between the United
                    States and Japan, Mexico would neither directly nor indirectly be allied or
                    associated with Japan. A similar appropriate expression of appreciation may be
                    informally conveyed by you to the Minister of War. You will understand that no
                    publicity for such a message should emanate from any source.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
